    "summary": "Razor‑sharp Garcia leads, standout High Time and The Other One",
    "blurb": "The set delivers razor‑sharp Jerry leads with highlights such as High Time, The Other One → Cosmic Charlie, and a vibrant China Cat Sunflower. Tom Constanten’s final show adds colorful keyboards despite occasional muddiness. The soundboard capture is clear, crisp and well‑balanced.",
    "review": "On January 30, 1970 at The Warehouse the Dead were in an early‑70 groove that feels both organized‑chaos and mellowly tight. Jerry Garcia’s leads are described as razor‑sharp, cutting through a set that swings from the driving rock of Casey Jones to the acoustic beauty of Easy Wind. Tom Constanten makes his last appearance on keyboards, shining brightly on China Cat Sunflower and High Time even if his parts get a little muddied elsewhere. The Other One rolls into Cosmic Charlie with a seamless transition that showcases the band’s telepathic interplay, while Black Peter and High Time provide soulful depth. This solid soundboard recording captures the full show with good clarity, making it an essential listen for fans of this transitional era.",
